> 
> ## 3. Create `universe_config.yml`
> 
> This contains strategy and universe-maintenance policy—not implementation details such as URLs or local cache paths.
> 
> ```yaml
> review:
>   # Evaluate this many stocks in each run.
>   sample_size: 100
> 
>   # At most this many of the evaluated stocks can be recommended.
>   max_recommendations: 20
> 
>   # A recommended stock must be among this proportion of the evaluated set.
>   top_fraction: 0.20
> 
>   # Do not re-review ordinary candidates for this many days.
>   candidate_review_after_days: 180
> 
>   # Current active holdings/tracked securities get reviewed more often.
>   current_stock_review_after_days: 60
> 
> universe:
>   # Prevent uncontrolled growth of stocks.yml.
>   max_active_stocks: 1000
> 
> eligibility:
>   min_price: 5.0
>   min_history_days: 180
>   min_trading_frequency: 0.95
>   min_median_daily_dollar_volume: 10000000
> 
>   # Scores below this always fail, regardless of relative rank.
>   min_absolute_score: 1.0
> 
>   liquidity_lookback_days: 60
> 
> scoring:
>   # Scores are weighted percentile-style components.
>   liquidity_weight: 0.60
>   trading_frequency_weight: 0.20
>   history_weight: 0.10
>   price_weight: 0.10
> ```
> 
> ETFs are intentionally allowed. The system excludes obvious non-stock/non-ETF instruments such as warrants, rights, units, preferred shares, and bonds.
> 
